{"name":"Tête-à-Tête","hex":"#d90166","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tête-à-tête","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A face-to-face meeting, or private conversation between two people, usually in an intimate setting; a head-to-head.","A bench or sofa that allows two people to talk face-to-face, especially one that is S-shaped."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In private, between two people; head-to-head."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tête à Tête (opera company)","blocks":[{"text":"Tête à Tête is an opera company based in Cornwall that currently operates in Cornwall, London and North-East England. Its primary mission is to reach new audiences, support artists' development, and to extend the boundaries of traditional opera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_opera_company.jpg/330px-T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_opera_company.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_(opera_company)"},{"title":"Tête-à-Tête (Art Pepper and George Cables album)","blocks":[{"text":"Tête-à-Tête is a duet album by saxophonist Art Pepper and pianist George Cables, recorded in 1982 and released on the Galaxy label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cf/T%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-T%C3%AAte_%28art_Pepper_and_George_Cables_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-T%C3%AAte_(Art_Pepper_and_George_Cables_album)"},{"title":"Tête-à-Tête (Ruth Anderson and Annea Lockwood album)","blocks":[{"text":"Tête-à-Tête is a studio album by American composers Ruth Anderson and Annea Lockwood. It was released by Ergot Records on April 28, 2023. Anderson and Lockwood became a couple shortly upon meeting in 1973 after the former took a sabbatical from her job and needed a replacement. The two would be together for a total of 50 years, wedding in 2005 in Canada following its legalization of same-sex marriage. During their relationship, Anderson composed \"Conversations,\" made as a gift to Lockwood in 1974; and \"Resolutions,\" her last electronic composition, in 1984. Anderson died of lung cancer in November 2019, prompting Lockwood to compose \"For Ruth\" as an official reply to \"Conversations\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/dd/Ruth_Anderson_and_Annea_Lockwood_-_T%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-T%C3%AAte.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-T%C3%AAte_(Ruth_Anderson_and_Annea_Lockwood_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_production.jpg/500px-T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_production.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_production.jpg/1280px-T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_production.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_production.jpg/500px-T%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_production.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 2022 production at the Cockpit Theatre, London","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AT%C3%AAte_%C3%A0_T%C3%AAte_production.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Portrait_of_Ruth_Anderson_Composer.png/500px-Portrait_of_Ruth_Anderson_Composer.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Portrait_of_Ruth_Anderson_Composer.png/500px-Portrait_of_Ruth_Anderson_Composer.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APortrait_of_Ruth_Anderson_Composer.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Annea_Lockwood_at_Constitution_Marsh_Sam_Green_Free_History_Project.jpg/500px-Annea_Lockwood_at_Constitution_Marsh_Sam_Green_Free_History_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Annea_Lockwood_at_Constitution_Marsh_Sam_Green_Free_History_Project.jpg/1280px-Annea_Lockwood_at_Constitution_Marsh_Sam_Green_Free_History_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Annea_Lockwood_at_Constitution_Marsh_Sam_Green_Free_History_Project.jpg/500px-Annea_Lockwood_at_Constitution_Marsh_Sam_Green_Free_History_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnnea_Lockwood_at_Constitution_Marsh_Sam_Green_Free_History_Project.jpg"}],"sounds":{"tête-à-tête":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/33/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/33/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/33/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte.wav.ogg"}]}}}